TITLE Add sulfuric acid in cumulative steps to pure water at pH 7.0
# Steps represent cumulative totals: 0.001, 0.005, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1 mol total
# So increments are: 0.001, 0.004, 0.005, 0.04, 0.05 mol

SOLUTION 1
    pH 7.0
    temp 25
    units mol/L

REACTION 1
    H2SO4  1
    0.001 moles

REACTION 2
    H2SO4  1
    0.004 moles

REACTION 3
    H2SO4  1
    0.005 moles

REACTION 4
    H2SO4  1
    0.04 moles

REACTION 5
    H2SO4  1
    0.05 moles

USE solution 1
USE reaction 1
SAVE solution 2
END

USE solution 2
USE reaction 2
SAVE solution 3
END

USE solution 3
USE reaction 3
SAVE solution 4
END

USE solution 4
USE reaction 4
SAVE solution 5
END

USE solution 5
USE reaction 5
SAVE solution 6
END

USE solution 6
SELECTED_OUTPUT
    -file selected_output3.txt
    -reset false
    -si H2(g)
END
